"Planning the cheapest route Delhi→Mumbai via Jaipur: the Jaipur→Mumbai part must itself be the cheapest from Jaipur.",
"Fibonacci: naive recursion recomputes F(k) many times (O(2ⁿ)). DP stores F(0..n) in a table: F(n)=F(n−1)+F(n−2) computed once each ⇒ O(n).",
["Needs optimal substructure and overlapping sub-problems.","Top-down (memoization) vs bottom-up (tabulation).","Steps: define sub-problem, recurrence, base case, fill table, reconstruct answer.","Trades memory for time.","Examples: 0/1 knapsack, LCS, chain matrix, Floyd–Warshall, making change.","Different from greedy: tries all sub-problem options."],
["Principle statement.","Memoization vs tabulation.","Fibonacci example."],
["State the principle.","Identify DP suitability.","Convert recursion to DP."],
["Using DP without overlapping sub-problems (no benefit).","Assuming greedy and DP are the same."],
[E("conceptual","Explain principle of optimality with an example.","Optimal substructure; shortest path via an intermediate vertex."),
 E("difference","Memoization vs tabulation.","Top-down recursion with cache vs bottom-up table filling.")],
[Q("MCQ","DP needs:","Optimal substructure + overlapping sub-problems","",["Only greedy choice","Optimal substructure + overlapping sub-problems","Random choice","Sorting"]),
 Q("true/false","Memoization is top-down.","True",""),
 Q("problem solving","DP time for Fibonacci(n).","O(n)",""),
 Q("short answer","Name two DP problems.","0/1 knapsack and LCS.",""),
 Q("comparison","DP vs D&C.","DP reuses overlapping sub-problems; D&C sub-problems are independent.","")],
"Optimality: optimal solution built from optimal sub-solutions; DP = optimal substructure + overlapping sub-problems; memoize or tabulate.",
problemStatement="Solve problems with optimal substructure and repeating sub-problems efficiently.",
approach="Store each sub-problem's answer once and reuse it.",
algorithmSteps=["1. Characterise the optimal structure.","2. Write a recurrence with base cases.","3. Fill the table bottom-up (or memoise top-down).","4. Reconstruct the solution from the table."],
pseudocode="Fib(n)\n  F[0]←0; F[1]←1\n  for i ← 2 to n do F[i] ← F[i−1] + F[i−2]\n  return F[n]",
